Let the two numbers be $x$ and $y$, where $x>y$.
We can set up a system of equations based on the given information:
\begin{align*}
x+y &= 22 \\
x-y &= 4
\end{align*}
We can solve this system by adding the two equations together:
\begin{align*}
(x+y) + (x-y) &= 22 + 4 \\
2x &= 26 \\
x &= 13
\end{align*}
Therefore, the greater of the two numbers is $\boxed{13}$.The answer is: 13

