Let $x$ be the number of one dollar bills and $y$ be the number of two dollar bills.
We can set up a system of equations:
\begin{align*}
x + y &= 49, \\
x + 2y &= 66.
\end{align*}
Solving this system, we can subtract the first equation from the second to eliminate $x$:
\begin{align*}
x + 2y - (x + y) &= 66 - 49, \\
y &= 17.
\end{align*}
Substituting this value of $y$ back into the first equation, we can solve for $x$:
\begin{align*}
x + 17 &= 49, \\
x &= 32.
\end{align*}
Therefore, James has $\boxed{32}$ one dollar bills.The answer is: 32

