draw(A--A + B);
draw(A--C);
draw(A + B--C,dashed);

label("$\mathbf{a}$", A, N);
label("$\mathbf{b}$", B, NW);
label("$\mathbf{a} \times (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c}) + \mathbf{b}$", A + B, NE);
label("$\mathbf{c}$", C, E);
[/asy]

Let $\theta$ be the angle between $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{c}$.
Then the magnitude of $\mathbf{a} \times (\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c}) + \mathbf{b}$ is
\begin{align*}
\|\mathbf{a}\| \|\mathbf{c}\| \sin \theta &= \|\mathbf{b}\| \\
\|\mathbf{c}\| \sin \theta &= 1 \\
2 \sin \theta &= 1 \\
\sin \theta &= \frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}Since $0^\circ \le \theta \le 180^\circ$, the smallest possible angle $\theta$ is $\boxed{30^\circ}$.The answer is: 30

