The probability that all six dice show different numbers is $\frac{6}{6} \cdot \frac{5}{6} \cdot \frac{4}{6} \cdot \frac{3}{6} \cdot \frac{2}{6} \cdot \frac{1}{6} = \frac{720}{6^6}$.
Therefore, the probability that at least two dice show the same number is equal to $1 - \frac{720}{6^6} = 1 - \frac{720}{46656} = 1 - \frac{5}{324} = \boxed{\frac{319}{324}}$.
